==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Hanzo''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Hanzo''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hanzo is one of the best [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]]/[[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] Ubers in the game. Due to most [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]]' high knockback counts, they often have difficulty reaching him, typically getting knocked back every hit. His moderate speed is well-suited for his role, allowing meatshields to regain ground while enemies are frozen. Even if enemies reach Hanzo, his high knockback count usually allows him to stay alive until victory on stages with his targeted traits.

As for [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], he works similarly except against high-range bulky bosses against whom his knockback count acts against him as he may get stunlocked to death. Aside from this potential weakness, he will destroy most [[The Face|Faces]], [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Buns]] and [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclones]] a cakewalk, especially when paired with [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]].

Hanzo's [[Colossus Slayer]] ability is also a pretty nice contribution to his versatility, making him a very valuable unit to have compared to a large number of Ubers who only have one single-trait ability and average stats.

Hanzo's 4.6k DPS at level 30 is slightly better than [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]]; however, his health is around 3x higher, which gives him far better survivability. As such, it's recommended to use Hanzo over Ururun unless knockback is needed or you're playing [[Restriction Stage]] that don't allow Ubers.

Two of his abilities that are often overlooked are his Slow and Freeze Immunities. These immunities make him even better against certain enemies he targets, like [[I.M. Phace]], [[Maawth]], and multiple [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus enemies]]. Additionally, he can be used as a good backliner in stages with [[Croakley]] or [[Henry]] (especially in stages like [[Conservation Society]]) without much trouble from them.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Hanzo's improvements in his [[True Form]] are considerably simpler than average, but they still serve him well. By receiving a sizeable damage and health buff, Hanzo goes from an already great unit to a stand out in his niche, being able to dish out a whole 5.4k DPS from a solid range of 450 with a fast attack that virtually guarantees Hanzo will hit his target. With its uptime jumping from 39% to 47%, Hanzo's freeze functions better to create breathing room for himself and the rest of your army, improving his performance against target traits.

Overall the lack of significant boosts to his abilities only goes to show the power of pre-TF Hanzo. As he is already a great unit from the start, Hanzo's True Form only gives him marginal boosts, but it is enough to reinforce his place in the meta. As a bonus, the evolution cost is also quite cheap for an Uber.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Wave]]''' is a real looker, and does live up to expectations, as it adds extra DPS whilst extending his Freeze's effective reach to 733! Though it only has a 50% activation rate, Hanzo attacks very quickly, which means it will be consistently proccing. Definitely worth its weight in NP.

'''[[Immune to Weaken]]''' has only two noteworthy matchups: those being [[Dark Dober]] and [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]], whose status effects are notoriously powerful and have nearly full uptime. If you're struggling with either of them, it is worth considering.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Curse]]''' is not good. It is intended for [[Lowkey]] and [[Golem Sunfish]] primarily, but doesn't do much to help in either matchup.

Finally, '''Attack Buff''' is obviously good on a nuker like Hanzo, but '''HP Buff''' not so much, as he relies on outranging threats.

